1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:10.000
For the kingdom of heaven is like a landowner, who went out early in the morning to hire workers for his vineyard.

2
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:15.990
He agreed to pay them a denarius for the day and sent them into his vineyard.

3
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:31.680
About nine in the morning, he went out and saw others standing in the marketplace doing nothing.

4
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:39.000
He told them, You also go and work in my vineyard, and I will pay you whatever is right.

5
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.300
So they went.

6
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:49.580
He went out again about noon and about three in the afternoon and did the same thing.

7
00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:57.670
About five in the afternoon, he went out and found still others standing around.

8
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:04.000
He asked them, Why have you been standing here all day long doing nothing?

9
00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:06.730
Because no one has hired us, they answered.

10
00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:12.000
He said to them, You also go and work in my vineyard.

11
00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:17.000
When evening came, the owner of the vineyard said to his foreman,

12
00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:24.000
Call the workers and pay them their wages, beginning with the last ones hired and going on to the first.

13
00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:29.990
The workers who were hired about five in the afternoon came and each received a denarius.

14
00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:35.640
So when those came who were hired first, they expected to receive more.

15
00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.680
But each one of them also received a denarius.

16
00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:44.690
When they received it, they began to grumble against the landowner.

17
00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:49.000
These who were hired last worked only one hour, they said.

18
00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:55.000
And you have made them equal to us who have borne the burden of the work and the heat of the day.

19
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.670
But he answered one of them, I am not being unfair to you, friend.

20
00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.680
Didn't you agree to work for a denarius?

21
00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:06.540
Take your pay and go.

22
00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:11.630
I want to give the one who was hired last the same as I gave you.

23
00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:16.590
Don't I have the right to do what I want with my own money?

24
00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:20.640
Or are you envious because I am generous?

25
00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:26.990
So the last will be first and the first will be last.
